>> title: Green Beans
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: green beans, pork, southern, stew, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: string beans, snap beans, pole beans, green beans with pork, southern green beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 20 min
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, fried-chicken, meatloaf
>> step.1: Stew these for an hour rather than blanching them for seven minutes. Green beans on this list are not meant to squeak, and the ones that do belong to somebody else's kitchen.
>> step.2: trim the stem ends off
>> step.3: render 8 min
>> step.4: sweat 5 min
>> step.5: stew covered 55 min
>> step.6: season at the end

Stew these for an hour rather than blanching them for seven minutes. Green beans on this list are not meant to squeak, and the ones that do belong to somebody else's kitchen.

Trim @green beans{2%lb}(900 g), snapping the stem ends off and leaving them whole.

Render @salt pork{4%oz}(115 g; diced) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~render{8%min}.

Sweat @&(~1)salt pork{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced) for ~sweat{5%min}.

Stew @&(~1)pork base{}, @&(~3)trimmed beans{} covered with @ham hock stock{1%qt}(950 mL), @black pepper{1%tsp} for ~stew{55%min}.

Season @&(~1)beans{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @cider vinegar{1%tsp}.

Drain nothing off. The liquid in the pot is half of what the side is, and it goes into the bowl with the beans.
